+# Tool input validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+Tool calls are checked at the registry boundary so malformed model input is returned to the model as a useful tool result before any executor runs.
+
+## Registry boundary
+
+- A call whose input violates the registered JSON Schema returns a `ToolResponse` describing the failed property and constraint, does not expose the offending value, and never invokes the executor ([validated by: returns a redacted schema failure and never invokes the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L15)).
+
+- A schema-valid object is passed to the executor unchanged, including unlisted properties, and the executor runs exactly once ([validated by: passes valid input and an unlisted property through unchanged exactly once](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L35)).
+
+- A static schema is compiled when its tool is registered, so repeated malformed calls are rejected and an uncompilable schema names its tool in the registration error ([validated by: compiles static schemas at registration and rejects every malformed call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L54)).
+
+- A function-valued definition is resolved and validated per call, so a schema that changes between calls is not replaced by a stale cached schema ([validated by: validates a function-valued definition against the schema resolved for that call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L80)).
